byBpcyBuZWFyLg=="}
Which neighbour definition suits point data such as facilities?

- Queen contiguity (shared border or corner)
- Rook contiguity (shared border only)
- k-nearest neighbours or a distance band
- Neighbours by alphabetical block name
:::

::: {.quiz-q data-qid="sw3" data-type="mcq" data-hash="f4sn3q.uav5fy" data-show="SXRzIGxhZyBpcyB1bmRlZmluZWQ7IHRlc3RzIG1heSBmYWlsIG9yIG1pc2xlYWQ=" data-explain="QW4gaXNvbGF0ZSBoYXMgbm8gbmVpZ2hib3VycyB0byBhdmVyYWdlOyBsb29rIGZvciBpc29s
YXRlcyAoemVyby5wb2xpY3kpIGFuZCBkZWNpZGUgaG93IHRvIGhhbmRsZSB0aGVtLCB0aGVu
IHJlcG9ydCBpdC4="}
An island block has no neighbours. Why does that matter?

- It doubles the weight of every other block
- Its lag is undefined; tests may fail or mislead
- Moran's I then drops to zero
- It must be deleted from the data before any test
:::

